// function-visibility commit 1.  The established compiler RESOLVES A CALL AGAINST THE
// DECLARATIONS VISIBLE AT THAT CALL.  Our frontend is two-pass, so before
// this every declaration in the unit was visible from everywhere.  Measured
// against the established compiler, sce_fp_rsx.  No defaults appear in any of these - the
// rule is observable without them.
//
// REFUSAL: a forward call with NO prior prototype.  The established compiler gives
// error C1008 "undefined variable"; we used to reach forward and compile it.
// Pinned by VERDICT - C1008 calls a function an undefined VARIABLE, and
// pinning that text would encode its confusion rather than its rule.

float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return helper(t); }
float4 helper(float4 c) { return c * 2.0; }
